* 3 1/2 cups all purpose or white whole wheat flour
* 4 teaspoons baking powder
* 1 teaspoon salt
* 2/3 cup butter
* 1 cup plus 1 tablespoon milk
* 1/2 cup maple syrup";}i:2;i:89;}i:15;a:3:{i:0;s:7:"p_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:269;}i:16;a:3:{i:0;s:6:"p_open";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:269;}i:17;a:3:{i:0;s:5:"cdata";i:1;a:1:{i:0;s:793:"1. Preheat oven; grease baking pan.
2. Combine the flour, nuts, baking powder and salt in a large bowl; mix well. 
3. Using a pastry blender or 2 forks, cut in the butter in small pieces till mixture resembles coarse crumbs.
4. Add the milk and 6 tablespoons of maple syrup. to the dry ingredients. Mix till the mixture clings together and forms a soft dough.
5. Turn the dough out on a lightly floured surface and knead 4 to 5 times lightly. Divide the dough in half, and pat or roll out a piece to a 7 inch round.
6. Cut round into 4 wedges, and place on pan, Repeat with the other round.
7. Prick the tops of the scones all over with a fork  and brush tops of scones with 2 tablespoons maple syrup.
8. Bake till golden brown, about 15 to 18 minutes. Cool scones on wire rack for 10 minutes.";}i:2;i:271;}i:18;a:3:{i:0;s:7:"p_close";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1064;}i:19;a:3:{i:0;s:12:"document_end";i:1;a:0:{}i:2;i:1064;}}